@startuml scoring-sentence
' SentenceScorer: the three views of one sentence's probability, and which of them the
' ranking helpers actually consume. log_prob is length-biased (it is a SUM, so longer
' sentences score lower); normalized_log_prob and perplexity divide the bias out.
' rank_sentences / best_sentence deliberately rank by the RAW log_prob — the dashed
' advisory edge marks the length-invariant scores a caller should use instead when the
' candidates differ in length.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/scoring-sentence.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/components/scoring/overview.md and
' docs/api/scoring.md (the SentenceScorer section).
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Sentence scoring — SentenceScorer over an n-gram model

rectangle "**candidate sentences**\nW⁽¹⁾ … W⁽ᵏ⁾, lengths N₁ … N_k" as cands #546E7A

rectangle "**log_prob(W)**\nΣᵢ log ℙ(wᵢ | hᵢ)\n**length-biased** (a sum)" as raw #1565C0
rectangle "**normalized_log_prob(W)**\n(1/N) · Σᵢ log ℙ(wᵢ | hᵢ)\nlength-invariant" as norm #1565C0
rectangle "**perplexity(W)**\nexp( −normalized_log_prob )\nlength-invariant" as ppl #1565C0

rectangle "**rank_sentences**\nsorted by log_prob, descending" as rank #455A64
rectangle "**best_sentence**\nargmax log_prob" as best #455A64

cands --> raw
raw --> norm : ÷ N
norm --> ppl : exp(−·)

raw --> rank
raw --> best

norm .[#2E7D32,dashed].> rank : prefer when\nlengths differ
ppl .[#2E7D32,dashed].> best : prefer when\nlengths differ

note bottom of raw #E3F2FD
  Every log ℙ(wᵢ | hᵢ) < 0, so appending a
  word can only //lower// log_prob. Comparing
  unequal-length candidates by log_prob
  therefore systematically favours the
  shortest one.
end note

note bottom of ppl #E3F2FD
  Equal-length candidates (spelling variants
  of one sentence) rank identically under all
  three scores — the bias only bites when N
  differs.
end note

legend right
  | Colour | Role |
  |<#546E7A> | caller-supplied candidates |
  |<#1565C0> | scores computed by the n-gram model |
  |<#455A64> | ranking helpers (rank by raw log_prob) |
  |<#2E7D32> | advisory: length-invariant alternative |
endlegend
@enduml
